WEBVTT

00:01:32.062 --> 00:01:34.064
<i>Our team got them.</i>

00:01:34.356 --> 00:01:37.443
<i>Right. Aiko Tachibana and the boy.</i>

00:01:39.236 --> 00:01:43.616
I keep telling you.
Bring the girl over here now.

00:01:44.491 --> 00:01:47.620
<i>There aren't proper facilities in Tokyo.</i>

00:01:47.786 --> 00:01:49.121
Are you still on this?

00:01:49.204 --> 00:01:51.206
-And what about you?
-What?

00:01:51.415 --> 00:01:54.627
<i>When are you going to</i>
<i>burn down that red river?</i>

00:01:54.877 --> 00:01:57.129
I don't know how you can say that.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.424
You know full well how many
assets are stranded

00:02:00.633 --> 00:02:05.971
in that area
the Malignant Matter has overtaken.

00:02:06.055 --> 00:02:09.183
In fact, the very Matter
is arguably a national asset

00:02:09.266 --> 00:02:12.269
with incredible value
as a subject for research.

00:02:12.394 --> 00:02:16.148
<i>An asset?</i>
<i>Enough to risk all of humanity for?</i>

00:02:16.231 --> 00:02:18.776
Yes, in order to save us from this crisis.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.653
<i>Such a roundabout method.</i>

00:02:20.986 --> 00:02:23.697
<i>Anyway, what are you doing</i>
<i>about Yuya Kanzaki?</i>

00:02:23.906 --> 00:02:25.324
We'll question him soon.

00:02:25.407 --> 00:02:28.619
<i>At any rate,</i>
<i>I would appreciate it if you didn't</i>

00:02:28.702 --> 00:02:30.537
<i>keep making me use my team.</i>

00:02:30.704 --> 00:02:33.374
<i>If we're inspected,</i>
<i>this will all be over.</i>

00:02:38.754 --> 00:02:39.671
Feeling better?

00:02:40.547 --> 00:02:43.092
Yes. Thank you.

00:02:44.635 --> 00:02:46.220
Are you with the police?

00:02:46.804 --> 00:02:50.474
Sort of. I work with
an agency involved with the Burst.

00:02:50.974 --> 00:02:52.142
NANAMI OZANAMI

00:02:52.976 --> 00:02:54.478
Did you come to my home?

00:02:55.312 --> 00:02:57.689
You slipped right through our fingers.

00:02:58.524 --> 00:02:59.483
I'm sorry.

00:02:59.942 --> 00:03:04.029
Dr. Isazu from Kiryu Hospital
requested that we protect you.

00:03:04.988 --> 00:03:07.783
Can I see Dr. Isazu?
I have some questions I...

00:03:09.743 --> 00:03:10.786
Never mind.

00:03:11.745 --> 00:03:15.249
It's late. I'll take you
to see him when things quiet down.

00:03:15.999 --> 00:03:17.376
Thank you.

00:03:19.336 --> 00:03:23.173
Who is that transfer student
who took me away?

00:03:24.925 --> 00:03:27.720
We discovered the transfer papers
you submitted

00:03:28.345 --> 00:03:30.764
to the school were fraudulent.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.935
Who are you working for?
What's your objective?

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:37.604
Why did you kidnap Aiko Tachibana?

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.484
You don't know, do you?

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:46.071
How about some more juice?

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:48.991
So...

00:03:50.826 --> 00:03:53.912
everything he told me is a lie, isn't it?

00:03:54.872 --> 00:03:55.914
What did he say?

00:03:56.081 --> 00:03:57.040
That my...

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.007
That my mom and brother are alive.

00:04:07.009 --> 00:04:09.636
He said they're still alive
at Ground Zero!

00:04:16.685 --> 00:04:19.897
Unfortunately, after your father died
in the accident,

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.859
your mother and brother
were confirmed killed in the Burst.

00:04:24.318 --> 00:04:28.739
It's in the official records of the
Control Agency of Artificial Creatures.

00:04:31.617 --> 00:04:35.120
Why did you go to such lengths
to get near her?

00:04:37.414 --> 00:04:40.626
That's a special plane.
Could you please not touch it?

00:04:41.877 --> 00:04:44.004
It's important to my school club.

00:04:44.296 --> 00:04:48.091
If you really must have it,
I guess I could give it to you.

00:04:53.347 --> 00:04:54.890
If you've got questions,

00:04:54.973 --> 00:04:57.476
then hurry and take me to the station.

00:04:57.684 --> 00:04:59.603
You have to register me, right?

00:05:00.646 --> 00:05:04.233
Or is this the only place
you can do your questioning?

00:05:05.776 --> 00:05:09.363
Fine. We'll take you
to a more appropriate location.

00:05:10.113 --> 00:05:11.114
Yes! There it is!

00:05:11.198 --> 00:05:13.867
I knew that paper plane
would come in handy!

00:05:15.744 --> 00:05:17.996
<i>Welcome back, Director Nanbara.</i>

00:05:18.163 --> 00:05:19.081
<i>How are things?</i>

00:05:19.164 --> 00:05:21.458
The two countries involved
are cooperating,

00:05:21.542 --> 00:05:24.962
and the UN General Assembly
will denounce the situation.

00:05:25.045 --> 00:05:28.340
We are currently requesting support
from the U.S.

00:05:28.423 --> 00:05:31.343
DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

00:05:31.927 --> 00:05:34.471
I'm moving Aiko Tachibana to Tokyo.

00:05:34.555 --> 00:05:36.723
And Professor Isazu, too, of course.

00:05:37.266 --> 00:05:38.308
What?

00:05:38.892 --> 00:05:41.562
We were fortunate that we got her back.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.691
Artificial organism research
has long been the target

00:05:45.774 --> 00:05:48.735
of both foreign intelligence
and terrorist groups.

00:05:48.819 --> 00:05:52.573
We've known that since before
Toshihide Yura's essay.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:55.784
They have far better
research facilities there.

00:05:55.867 --> 00:05:59.705
Aiko Tachibana is not
the private property of Kiryu Research.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.083
If only the government
had seen the importance

00:06:03.166 --> 00:06:05.335
of building Cell Assemblers sooner,

00:06:05.419 --> 00:06:08.338
we would have the advantage, wouldn't we?

00:06:08.672 --> 00:06:10.173
That's painful to hear.

00:06:10.966 --> 00:06:11.967
My apologies.

00:06:14.011 --> 00:06:16.888
<i>We'll move Yuya Kanzaki</i>
<i>in Moriyama's vehicle.</i>

00:06:17.222 --> 00:06:19.558
<i>Take the set routes</i>
<i>to headquarters.</i>

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:20.934
Roger.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.020
-Excuse me!
-Yes?

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:26.106
Will I be able to see him again?

00:06:26.356 --> 00:06:29.109
He still needs to be dealt with properly.

00:06:41.663 --> 00:06:42.831
What's going on?

00:06:48.962 --> 00:06:50.547
You stay here!

00:06:52.341 --> 00:06:53.300
It's an attack!

00:07:03.393 --> 00:07:04.478
Wait!

00:07:06.063 --> 00:07:07.856
-Thanks!
-Get to Haruka's car!

00:07:08.023 --> 00:07:09.316
-Tachibana!
-Wait!

00:07:14.279 --> 00:07:15.405
There's more!

00:07:21.328 --> 00:07:23.789
An assault vehicle?
Are they government?

00:07:28.335 --> 00:07:30.045
-What?
-Kanzaki!

00:07:30.128 --> 00:07:31.254
Tachibana!

00:07:47.437 --> 00:07:48.981
Is it true?

00:07:51.733 --> 00:07:54.319
Are Mom and Ryota really alive?

00:07:55.195 --> 00:07:57.572
Those people said they were dead!

00:07:58.573 --> 00:08:00.242
What do you think?

00:08:00.492 --> 00:08:03.996
I don't know. But I hope they're alive!

00:08:05.497 --> 00:08:07.833
I want to believe that they're alive!

00:08:19.136 --> 00:08:20.178
Pull out!

00:08:29.021 --> 00:08:30.022
Damn!

00:08:32.399 --> 00:08:34.901
<i>This isn't just any mistake!</i>

00:08:34.985 --> 00:08:36.570
I'll handle this.

00:08:37.904 --> 00:08:39.406
I'll do it right now.

00:08:42.576 --> 00:08:44.453
Shall we involve state police?

00:08:45.287 --> 00:08:46.788
You know we can't.

00:08:51.376 --> 00:08:55.756
As everyone knows,
the Harinoki Tunnel in the east

00:08:56.089 --> 00:08:59.551
and the cable car tunnel
from Tateyama in the west

00:08:59.634 --> 00:09:02.220
have both been sealed off by the Matter.

00:09:02.804 --> 00:09:04.765
<i>Therefore, for this mission</i>

00:09:04.848 --> 00:09:07.434
<i>we have no choice but to take a route</i>

00:09:07.684 --> 00:09:10.687
<i>that follows the valley rail line</i>
<i>to Primary Point.</i>

00:09:11.396 --> 00:09:14.691
<i>In particular,</i>
<i>after we pass the gate at K2,</i>

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.110
<i>Area Three and beyond is uncharted.</i>

00:09:17.319 --> 00:09:19.529
<i>No Diver has entered and returned alive.</i>

00:09:20.155 --> 00:09:21.573
Evidence has no data,

00:09:21.656 --> 00:09:24.868
and we don't know what kind
of Matter we'll run into.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.995
This will be a rough mission.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.581
We already know that! What else?

00:09:30.415 --> 00:09:34.586
The mission commences
before dawn, at 4:30 a.m.

00:09:35.212 --> 00:09:37.589
Complete preparations one hour prior.

00:09:37.881 --> 00:09:40.842
Shiraishi has transported
all your equipment here.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.304
I know you guys can pull this off.

00:09:45.222 --> 00:09:46.431
I expect your best.

00:09:48.266 --> 00:09:49.309
-Wilco!
-Wilco!

00:10:04.032 --> 00:10:05.200
Hello, there.

00:10:06.368 --> 00:10:07.911
I'm Kazuki Minase.

00:10:08.829 --> 00:10:11.289
I'm Aiko Tachibana.

00:10:11.623 --> 00:10:13.458
Nice to meet you, Tachibana.

00:10:13.875 --> 00:10:17.671
The guy over there is my friend,
Yoshihiko Sagami.

00:10:18.171 --> 00:10:19.464
Nice to meet you.

00:10:21.424 --> 00:10:22.259
Hello.

00:10:22.342 --> 00:10:24.970
He's ex-special forces,
so he's super elite.

00:10:25.178 --> 00:10:27.764
And that over there is Kaede Misawa.

00:10:28.473 --> 00:10:29.891
She's a bitch.

00:10:30.934 --> 00:10:32.769
I can hear you!

00:10:33.228 --> 00:10:35.981
Kaede is just very frank.

00:10:36.064 --> 00:10:38.316
I'm Haruka Seri. Nice to meet you.

00:10:39.818 --> 00:10:41.486
It's nice to meet you, too.

00:10:42.737 --> 00:10:44.030
Tachibana.

00:10:44.614 --> 00:10:45.615
Come here.

00:10:47.367 --> 00:10:48.201
Yeah, sure.

00:10:49.703 --> 00:10:52.330
These are the rations for the mission.

00:10:52.455 --> 00:10:53.540
Rations?

00:10:53.623 --> 00:10:55.375
Portable meals.

00:10:56.084 --> 00:10:58.837
Try it out to see if you can stomach it.

00:10:59.421 --> 00:11:00.380
Okay.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.344
It's really good.

00:11:07.053 --> 00:11:08.096
Phew, that's good

00:11:08.179 --> 00:11:10.765
It's the usual stuff, isn't it?

00:11:11.683 --> 00:11:13.935
I swear I'll protect that girl.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.855
Yeah, yeah.
Make sure you protect me, too.

00:11:18.732 --> 00:11:21.568
A device that monitors my brain waves?

00:11:22.527 --> 00:11:23.862
It's a Mind Scanner.

00:11:24.195 --> 00:11:26.573
A Mind Scanner?

00:11:26.907 --> 00:11:30.201
Yes. I want you to put this
on your forehead.

00:11:35.457 --> 00:11:38.752
I have to get you to Primary Point

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.963
with your body and mind
in good, healthy condition.

00:11:42.047 --> 00:11:43.381
Hold on!

00:11:45.425 --> 00:11:47.761
This isn't a joke, right?

00:11:48.678 --> 00:11:50.347
We really are

00:11:51.264 --> 00:11:52.641
going into the Area...

00:11:55.518 --> 00:11:58.021
Yuya! There's trouble!

00:11:58.647 --> 00:11:59.689
It's the Matter!

00:12:00.315 --> 00:12:01.608
MAJOR MATTER ACTIVITY

00:12:01.691 --> 00:12:03.151
<i>I repeat,</i>

00:12:03.401 --> 00:12:07.697
<i>the Chief Cabinet Secretary</i>
<i>just held an emergency press conference</i>

00:12:07.781 --> 00:12:10.575
<i>announcing that major</i>
<i>Malignant Matter activity</i>

00:12:10.659 --> 00:12:13.411
<i>has been observed</i>
<i>in the contaminated area,</i>

00:12:13.495 --> 00:12:15.455
<i>also known as the Malignant Area.</i>

00:12:17.123 --> 00:12:21.378
<i>This is the most activity observed</i>
<i>since the Burst two years ago.</i>

00:12:21.878 --> 00:12:25.382
<i>Beyond promptly summoning</i>
<i>all related government officials</i>

00:12:25.507 --> 00:12:28.927
<i>to the Crisis Control Center</i>
<i>at the prime minister's home,</i>

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:33.014
<i>the government is establishing</i>
<i>an emergency disaster control center,</i>

00:12:33.473 --> 00:12:35.266
<i>and has stated the situation</i>

00:12:35.475 --> 00:12:38.270
<i>in and around the Area</i>
<i>is extremely precarious.</i>

00:12:39.437 --> 00:12:42.232
<i>At the request of the local government,</i>

00:12:42.565 --> 00:12:46.528
<i>the Self-Defense Forces is preparing</i>
<i>for disaster relief efforts.</i>

00:12:46.611 --> 00:12:51.074
<i>However, since this could entail use</i>
<i>of military force against the Matter,</i>

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.952
<i>it is believed that the government</i>

00:12:54.035 --> 00:12:57.664
<i>will enact the country's first ever</i>
<i>Civil Protection Order.</i>

00:12:57.747 --> 00:12:59.124
<i>In the wake of this,</i>

00:12:59.207 --> 00:13:03.294
<i>fierce protests by opposing</i>
<i>civic organizations is expected.</i>

00:13:04.045 --> 00:13:07.882
Nearly all remaining security cameras
in the Area have gone down.

00:13:08.842 --> 00:13:10.927
Crisis Control is launching drones.

00:13:11.011 --> 00:13:12.971
They will be useless.

00:13:13.596 --> 00:13:15.390
I told them the same thing.

00:13:19.602 --> 00:13:23.314
Self-Defense Forces vehicles
are now driving past me.

00:13:23.898 --> 00:13:27.694
They're holding tranquilizer missiles
to be fired at the Matter.

00:13:27.777 --> 00:13:29.279
<i>This screws things up.</i>

00:13:29.571 --> 00:13:31.614
<i>If security at the Gate is tightened,</i>

00:13:31.698 --> 00:13:34.909
even Divers could have trouble
getting into the Area.

00:14:17.786 --> 00:14:21.122
<i>Shiraishi's checking on</i>
<i>any activity near the Gate now.</i>

00:14:21.206 --> 00:14:24.376
Got it. I'll contact you
if anything happens.

00:14:26.336 --> 00:14:30.256
<i>The prime minister will back the</i>
<i>ruling party's Matter eradication faction.</i>

00:14:30.423 --> 00:14:31.841
<i>This will be a showdown.</i>

00:14:32.425 --> 00:14:33.551
<i>I'll say it again.</i>

00:14:33.802 --> 00:14:37.722
<i>The grand result of our research</i>
<i>is Aiko Tachibana. Next to her,</i>

00:14:37.806 --> 00:14:42.060
<i>the prototypes and samples</i>
<i>left inside the Area are mere trash.</i>

00:14:42.477 --> 00:14:46.189
When you say "our",
don't you mean just your allies?

00:14:46.773 --> 00:14:48.441
You don't understand.

00:14:48.566 --> 00:14:51.569
<i>Project ACO isn't just yours.</i>

00:14:51.736 --> 00:14:53.363
It's AICO.

00:14:53.446 --> 00:14:57.784
Artificial and Intelligent
Cellular Organism.

00:14:58.368 --> 00:15:00.203
You'd better not forget that

00:15:00.328 --> 00:15:04.999
Yura fundamentally transformed
this project due to Aiko Tachibana.

00:15:07.001 --> 00:15:09.421
Naho,
I'm visiting relatives for a while.

00:15:36.072 --> 00:15:37.949
-Aiko!
-Sister!

00:15:38.283 --> 00:15:39.784
Can you see us, Aiko?

00:15:42.287 --> 00:15:44.747
<i>What is this? Where am I?</i>

00:15:47.375 --> 00:15:50.378
<i>It's Dr. Isazu. Is this the hospital?</i>

00:15:50.962 --> 00:15:53.882
<i>Oh, right. I was in an accident.</i>

00:16:00.096 --> 00:16:02.265
Evacuate immediately!

00:16:04.434 --> 00:16:05.685
<i>I have to escape!</i>

00:16:10.648 --> 00:16:12.859
-Okay, you're all set.
-Take off!

00:16:35.798 --> 00:16:38.551
<i>What? I got away, didn't I?</i>

00:16:49.979 --> 00:16:51.272
<i>What's this?</i>

00:16:52.565 --> 00:16:53.691
<i>Who is that?</i>

00:16:55.318 --> 00:16:58.738
<i>A girl? No, it's Ryota!</i>

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.823
<i>His hair is so long.</i>

00:17:01.991 --> 00:17:03.326
<i>Mom!</i>

00:17:11.167 --> 00:17:13.294
Was I asleep?

00:17:13.711 --> 00:17:14.629
You were.

00:17:15.463 --> 00:17:19.133
I had a dream. Mom and Ryota were in it.

00:17:20.343 --> 00:17:22.762
It was like they really were alive.

00:17:23.555 --> 00:17:25.306
What you saw is reality.

00:17:25.598 --> 00:17:26.558
What?

00:17:26.724 --> 00:17:28.810
You actually saw that yourself.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.312
How can you know that?

00:17:31.813 --> 00:17:35.400
Right now,
you possess the ability to see that.

00:17:35.775 --> 00:17:37.777
-What?
-Remember what I told you?

00:17:38.528 --> 00:17:40.947
You're not a human right now.

00:17:45.994 --> 00:17:47.704
I can believe you, right?

00:17:48.037 --> 00:17:49.581
I can believe your story

00:17:49.664 --> 00:17:54.043
that if I go to Ground Zero,
I can save Mom and Ryota, right?

00:17:59.257 --> 00:18:03.094
I'm going! My family is still alive
and I'm going to save them!

00:18:07.181 --> 00:18:08.725
<i>Let's reconfirm.</i>

00:18:09.309 --> 00:18:10.602
<i>Once past the Gate,</i>

00:18:10.685 --> 00:18:14.188
<i>maintain radio silence</i>
<i>until reaching the first camp in K1.</i>

00:18:14.981 --> 00:18:17.150
<i>After that, with all the equipment</i>

00:18:17.734 --> 00:18:21.070
<i>stored at the camps by Divers</i>
<i>and CAAC Special Forces,</i>

00:18:21.154 --> 00:18:25.575
<i>the absolute longest</i>
<i>the whole mission can take is...</i>

00:18:26.451 --> 00:18:27.285
Ten days.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:28.870
One week.

00:18:30.622 --> 00:18:32.206
Stick exactly to the plan.

00:18:33.791 --> 00:18:35.585
She's losing consciousness?

00:18:35.835 --> 00:18:39.005
Is it the other Aiko Tachibana?
What's the cause?

00:18:39.339 --> 00:18:40.673
<i>I can't say.</i>

00:18:41.257 --> 00:18:44.427
But we must arrive
before she loses consciousness completely.

00:18:44.802 --> 00:18:47.889
<i>You're right.</i>
<i>I'll bolster our backup plans.</i>

00:18:48.222 --> 00:18:49.390
Thanks.

00:18:50.725 --> 00:18:52.685
Hey! Wait!

00:18:53.978 --> 00:18:55.438
Come back!

00:18:56.439 --> 00:18:57.398
I said wait!

00:19:00.068 --> 00:19:02.278
I told you I would put it on for you.

00:19:02.654 --> 00:19:03.988
Thank you.

00:19:05.198 --> 00:19:07.241
Don't rush it.
Let it grow on you.

00:19:07.325 --> 00:19:08.451
Okay.

00:19:08.868 --> 00:19:12.664
This isn't simply an undergarment.
It's your partner.

00:19:12.747 --> 00:19:16.376
It links with your muscles
to help you lift heavy objects,

00:19:16.459 --> 00:19:18.836
and protect you from physical shock.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.546
It's dangerous in the Area,

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.091
so we have to wear specialized suits.

00:19:23.675 --> 00:19:27.136
For now, until we get
the specialized vehicles in K1,

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:29.055
you'll wear the same suit as the Divers.

00:19:29.597 --> 00:19:32.975
There! Your Live Suit is good to go.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.896
And here's your nutriobags.

00:19:37.522 --> 00:19:41.818
Artificial organisms are living beings,
so they need to eat and excrete.

00:19:42.443 --> 00:19:44.195
Let's get these hooked up.

00:19:44.779 --> 00:19:45.822
<i>Let's not tell</i>

00:19:46.489 --> 00:19:50.076
the Divers about the link
between you and your duplicate.

00:19:50.159 --> 00:19:51.369
Really?

00:19:51.494 --> 00:19:54.872
Your body is a composite
of real and artificial parts,

00:19:55.164 --> 00:19:58.835
so you excrete bioactive substances
that attract the Matter.

00:19:59.502 --> 00:20:01.629
That is, the Matter is drawn to you.

00:20:01.713 --> 00:20:03.297
What? No way!

00:20:03.381 --> 00:20:04.716
Don't worry.

00:20:05.133 --> 00:20:08.136
I have a drug that will
suppress that bioactivity.

00:20:09.762 --> 00:20:12.265
Is that what
they gave me at the hospital?

00:20:12.849 --> 00:20:14.892
It's the same. Relax, it's safe.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.271
I don't want to worry the Divers.

00:20:19.397 --> 00:20:20.732
Okay.

00:20:22.608 --> 00:20:26.696
But that means Dr. Isazu knew

00:20:27.113 --> 00:20:28.948
about my body this whole time.

00:20:29.031 --> 00:20:30.950
He is a doctor, after all.

00:20:33.035 --> 00:20:33.995
Tachibana.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.747
Yes?

00:20:36.205 --> 00:20:39.250
I'm going to plug the connector
into your Live Suit.

00:20:39.333 --> 00:20:40.168
Okay.

00:20:40.251 --> 00:20:42.920
It measures your vitals and syncs to you.

00:20:43.004 --> 00:20:44.130
It'll feel weird.

00:20:48.676 --> 00:20:49.844
That so creepy!

00:20:50.428 --> 00:20:53.598
I know! It was the same
the first time I wore one.

00:20:53.765 --> 00:20:55.266
You'll get used to it.

00:20:57.685 --> 00:21:00.646
<i>Let's get through the Gate</i>
<i>before it's sealed off.</i>

00:21:07.195 --> 00:21:09.739
<i>We can't guarantee your safety in there.</i>

00:21:09.822 --> 00:21:14.160
<i>If I expected you to,</i>
<i>I would never be able to do this job.</i>

00:21:20.541 --> 00:21:23.294
<i>The tranquilizer missiles</i>
<i>have taken effect,</i>

00:21:23.377 --> 00:21:25.546
and the situation is quieting down,

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:28.758
but we have no idea
when it will become active again.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:32.094
We have received orders from Tokyo!

00:21:32.178 --> 00:21:35.473
<i>Orders as of 4:42 a.m.</i>
<i>Seal off Aimoto Dam!</i>

00:21:36.557 --> 00:21:39.393
Are you kidding?
We just let some guys through.

00:21:39.894 --> 00:21:42.772
<i>By order of the government,</i>

00:21:43.189 --> 00:21:46.150
<i>we will now be sealing off the dam.</i>

00:21:46.651 --> 00:21:51.823
<i>All Divers within the Area</i>
<i>must immediately evacuate.</i>

00:21:52.406 --> 00:21:53.574
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:21:54.408 --> 00:21:55.743
She's inside the Area?

00:21:55.827 --> 00:21:57.328
Apparently, yes.

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:19.141
All right, let's get moving.

00:23:57.281 --> 00:23:59.450
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
